WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:02.458
This is our first complete class example

00:00:03.382 --> 00:00:07.132
The class is named CustomerRecord By convention

00:00:07.316 --> 00:00:09.513
Python class names are often written using

00:00:09.526 --> 00:00:11.382
capital letters at the beginning of each

00:00:11.408 --> 00:00:14.553
word Inside the class we define a

00:00:14.579 --> 00:00:17.724
special method called dunder init Its written

00:00:17.737 --> 00:00:20.132
form uses two underscores before init and

00:00:20.158 --> 00:00:23.224
two underscores after it You will often

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:25.921
hear Python developers simply say dunder init

00:00:26.855 --> 00:00:28.605
The dunder init method runs when a

00:00:28.632 --> 00:00:31.895
new object is created In this example

00:00:32.092 --> 00:00:35.184
it receives self customer ID and segment

00:00:36.105 --> 00:00:38.039
The word self refers to the current

00:00:38.066 --> 00:00:41.224
object When we write self dot customer

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:43.934
ID equals customer ID we are storing

00:00:43.947 --> 00:00:46.566
the provided customer ID inside the object

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:49.592
The same idea applies to self dot

00:00:49.618 --> 00:00:53.553
segment Next the line that creates CustomerRecord

00:00:53.579 --> 00:00:55.421
with C one zero one and Retail

00:00:55.447 --> 00:00:58.816
creates one object That object is stored

00:00:58.842 --> 00:01:01.895
in the variable customer The final two

00:01:01.921 --> 00:01:04.658
print statements access the object's attributes
using

00:01:04.684 --> 00:01:07.290
customer dot customer ID and customer dot

00:01:07.316 --> 00:01:10.579
segment Before you run the code predict

00:01:10.605 --> 00:01:13.539
the output The customer ID should be

00:01:13.566 --> 00:01:15.605
C one zero one and the segment

00:01:15.632 --> 00:01:19.553
should be Retail Click Run now The

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:23.013
terminal should display those two values Now

00:01:23.026 --> 00:01:26.592
try creating a second object For example

00:01:26.776 --> 00:01:29.026
you could create another CustomerRecord with the

00:01:29.039 --> 00:01:30.908
ID C one zero two and the

00:01:30.921 --> 00:01:34.447
segment Business Then print the second object's

00:01:34.461 --> 00:01:37.408
attributes The key idea is that the

00:01:37.421 --> 00:01:39.868
class defines the structure while each object

00:01:39.895 --> 00:01:41.197
stores its own values
